From: arch-dotfiles, for hyprwm/xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland#431 (open, no upstream fix)
Subject: screencopy: skip stream state callbacks while the portal is torn down

unique_ptr::reset nulls m_sPortals.screencopy before ~CScreencopyPortal runs; its pw_core_disconnect calls
pwStreamStateChange for each live stream, which dereferenced the null portal: a segfault on every shutdown
with a screencast attached.

--- a/src/portals/Screencopy.cpp
+++ b/src/portals/Screencopy.cpp
@@ -907,6 +907,11 @@
 static void pwStreamStateChange(void* data, pw_stream_state old, pw_stream_state state, const char* error) {
     const auto PSTREAM = (CPipewireConnection::SPWStream*)data;
 
+    // the portal is being torn down: unique_ptr::reset nulls it before ~CScreencopyPortal, whose pw_core_disconnect
+    // calls back here for every live stream (hyprwm/xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland#431)
+    if (!g_pPortalManager->m_sPortals.screencopy)
+        return;
+
     PSTREAM->pSession->sharingData.nodeID         = pw_stream_get_node_id(PSTREAM->stream);
     PSTREAM->pSession->sharingData.pipewireSerial = readObjectSerial(PSTREAM->stream);
 
